-- title:
--   Ramification of X₁(M) over the j-line at finite j₀
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Write $F =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) $\kappa\, M$ for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the family `intFormRatiosC` $\kappa$ $(\Gamma_1(M))$, that is, by the ratios attached to integral modular forms on $\Gamma_1(M)$ reduced to $\kappa$. Let $J \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $\kappa$, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\kappa$ of the integral power series $E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-type numerator `jNum`, i.e. the $q$-expansion of $j$ over $\kappa$. Let $x$ be a place of $F$ over $\kappa$, given by a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\kappa$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, and let $\operatorname{ord}_x$ be the associated normalised integer valuation. Assume $\operatorname{ord}_x J \ge 0$, and let $j_0 \in \kappa$ satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_x\bigl(J - j_0\bigr) \ge 1$. Then $\operatorname{ord}_x(J - j_0)$ equals [`ModularCurve.jWidth`](def/ModularCurve_JWidth.html#L7) $j_0$, that is $3$ if $j_0 = 0$, $2$ if $j_0 = 1728$, and $1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the ramification statement for the covering $X_1(M) \to X(1)$ above a finite point $j = j_0$ of the $j$-line in characteristic $p \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$: every place of the function field lying over $j_0$ and finite for $J$ has ramification index $|\mathrm{Aut}(E_{j_0})|/2 \in \{3,2,1\}$, uniformly in the fibre. It is used in the analysis of places of $\kappa(X_1(M))$ at which reductions of weight-one forms and Hasse-invariant roots are studied, and in the local description of the valuation subrings of this function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ord_sub_algebraMap_eq_jWidth_of_place_x1FunctionFieldC.lean

